  "limitations": [
    "Matched tasks and decoding; existing controls were collected separately and are not contemporaneous controls.",
    "No compute-matched causal interpretation: Piotr/adaptive use two GPUs per shard; random/likelihood use one.",
    "Likelihood is mean base-policy log probability of generated response tokens, not calibrated action correctness.",
    "Exploratory original gate: the cutoff was derived from 278 saved final-decision responses on the SAME 300 evaluation tasks; calibration was outcome-blind but not task-independent and was biased toward late/terminal decisions. This is neither calibrated action correctness nor a noninferiority claim. Observed online gating need not equal 25 percent.",
    "Invalid and unjudged outcomes remain zero in all300 denominators; valid-only rates are descriptive.",
    "Paired task bootstrap does not capture across-run variability, website drift or judge error; intervals are not multiplicity-adjusted.",
    "Request seeds are recorded but FlashInfer does not promise identical prefixes or batch-independent determinism.",
    "Generated-token compute proxy excludes prefill, attention, vision, cache and log-probability computation.",
    "Metered failed physical attempts are included; unmetered failures and interrupted unsaved work remain explicit limitations.",
    "Historical control accounting is reused for context and is not charged again to these new approvals."
  ],
